-- title:
--   Multidegree lies in the image of the intersection pairing
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\neq 0$ and a prime $p$ with $p\nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak P$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package for level $N_0p$ over $R=$ `DRLevel.R p`, with structure morphism `DRLevel.toBase N₀ p` and cusp section $\mathfrak P.\varepsilon_{\inf}$. Let $D$ be a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation for this morphism (a scheme over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ with a zero section) and let $hD$ witness that $D$ represents the condition `algEquivZeroCut`, i.e. that its Poincaré bundle is a rigidified line bundle whose fibres at algebraically closed points are algebraically equivalent to zero, and that every such rigidified bundle on a base $T$ is the pullback of the Poincaré bundle along a unique $T$-point of $D$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O:R\to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, with fraction field $K$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with a surjective ring map $O\to\kappa$; let $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ be a resolved model package $Y\to \mathfrak X_O$ over $O$ relative to these data, with component ideal sheaves `comp w` indexed by `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width`. Let $z$ be an $O$-point of $D$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\rho_O$, let $\sigma_0,\dots,\sigma_{m-1}$ be sections of $Y\to\operatorname{Spec} O$, let $\mathrm{pos},\mathrm{neg}:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\mathbb N$ with $\sum_j(\mathrm{pos}\,j-\mathrm{neg}\,j)=0$, and let $v_j$ record the component of the special fibre containing the closed point of $\sigma_j$, in the sense that this point lies in the support of `comp (v j)` and in the support of no other component ideal. Assume the pullback to $Y\times_{\operatorname{Spec} O}\operatorname{Spec} K$ of the pullback along $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}$ of the line bundle $(hD.\mathrm{poincare}.\mathrm{pullbackAlong}\ z).L$ is isomorphic to the iterated tensor product, over $j$ in $\mathrm{Fin}\,m$, of `sectionTwist` of $\sigma_j$ with exponent $\mathrm{pos}\,j$ tensored with the module of the $\mathrm{neg}\,j$-th power of the section ideal of $\sigma_j$, folded against the unit module. Then the function $w\mapsto\sum_j[\,v_j=w\,](\mathrm{pos}\,j-\mathrm{neg}\,j)$ on `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width` lies in the range of the additive endomorphism `intersectionAlpha` of the intersection table `x0MqResolvedTable 𝔛reg.width`, namely $c\mapsto\bigl(j\mapsto\sum_i c_i\,\mathrm{inter}(i,j)\bigr)$ for the adjacency-minus-degree matrix of the dual graph of the resolved special fibre.
--
--   This is the multidegree obstruction of the Mazur–Rapoport type for an $O$-point of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of $X_0(N_0p)$ whose generic fibre is given by a divisor supported in $O$-sections: the vector of multiplicities attached to the components of the resolved special fibre must be an intersection-pairing image. It feeds the component-group computation, being cited in the proof that the relevant component class vanishes under the hypotheses of the specialisation argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRResolvedModelPackageLevel_multidegree_mem_range_intersectionAlpha_of_pullbackAlong_generic_iso_of_surjective.lean

